# Shell scripts are LF in the working tree on every platform, whatever a
# developer's core.autocrlf says. Development happens on Windows as well as
# in the Ubuntu VM (CLAUDE.md), and a CRLF checkout of packaging/install.sh
# or packaging/linux/*.sh is not a cosmetic difference there: the shell reads
# the carriage return as part of the command and the script dies on its first
# line with "bash\r: No such file or directory". The release workflow runs
# these files, so that failure would surface as a release that builds no
# artifacts.
*.sh text eol=lf
